# P18-V01 heartbeat request-header parity slice — 2026-10-17T22:38:27Z

- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Java behavior oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 source commit
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; external Java checkout remained
  read-only. Its pre-existing untracked `broker/src/test/java/org/apache/rocketmq/broker/aaaa.java` was preserved.
- Audited pinned `MQClientAPIImpl.sendHeartbeat` and `sendHeartbeatV2`: both
  construct `HeartbeatRequestHeader`, an `RpcRequestHeader` subtype with
  inherited nullable `ns`, `nsd`, `bname`, and `oway` fields. Rust had been
  using the empty Lite subscription control header, which retained the default
  empty wire map but omitted the public Java header surface.
- Added/exported Rust `HeartbeatRequestHeader`, inherited RPC field encoding,
  getters/setters (including deprecated bname aliases), Java equality/hash,
  integer `hashCode` and `toString` behavior. Both heartbeat RPCs now use the
  typed header. Added pinned Java typed frame and request-header identity data,
  and registered the type in the Rust header inventory.
- First `mvn verify` attempt stopped because the newly registered Rust fixture
  generator ran before Maven's Java header-fixture generation. Generated the
  Java 5.5.1 fixture first with `mvn compile exec:java`, then reran `verify`;
  it completed the 37-scenario suite, fixture checks, 56 typed-header
  cross-decodes and 14 typed-body cross-decodes without errors.
- First focused Rust header-inventory compile found an incorrect relative path
  to `request-header-identity.json`; corrected it and reran successfully.
- Verification passed:
  - `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --test header_inventory`
    (3 tests).
  - `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-protocol request_header_equality_and_hash_match_rpc_base_fields` (1 test).
  - `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-core --test extensions` (14 tests).
  - `cargo clippy --locked -p rocketmq-classic-protocol -p rocketmq-classic-core --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`.
  - Maven `verify`: all 37 scenarios, fixture drift checks, Rust/Java header and
    body cross-decodes.
